    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2T63Kp9dkm1NruXo3BFatDY)_\n\n**Problem:** Dirvish listed two sets of icons per entry.\n\n**Cause:** `sp-dired` gives Dirvish its own icons (`nerd-icons` in `dirvish-attributes`). `sp-icons` also turns on `nerd-icons-dired-mode` from `dired-mode-hook`. Dirvish buffers are derived from dired, so that hook ran in them too and both drew an icon.\n\n**Change:** `sp-icons--dired-off-in-dirvish` turns `nerd-icons-dired-mode` off from `dirvish-mode-hook` and `dirvish-directory-view-mode-hook` (parent and preview windows). Plain dired keeps its icons. Module doc and CHANGELOG updated.\n\n**Not checked:** nothing was run (no Emacs with Dirvish and nerd-icons in the container). If `dirvish-mode` turns out to be enabled before `dired-mode-hook` runs, the order matters and this needs a look.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01YC6cQX83mE1cB3KHqwciG9)_",
